{"instruction": "Build a 3D torus knot showcase", "input": "Single-file HTML, Three.js r128 via CDN. A centerpiece TorusKnotGeometry(1.1, 0.32, 220, 40, 2, 3) with MeshStandardMaterial { metalness: 0.92, roughness: 0.18 } in gold 0xd4af37, castShadow, slowly rotating. Around it, orbit particles: ~28 small metallic spheres on randomized tilted orbits (userData { radius 2.6-4.2, speed ±0.3-1.3, ph, tilt }) that move with cos/sin in the loop. Buttons: Cycle Color steps a 5-color palette (gold/cyan/pink/green/lavender) via material.color.setHex; Spin toggles the knot rotation. Ring lights + fill lights, starfield, OrbitControls with damping, resize handler.", "output": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>🌀 3D Torus Knot</title>\n<style>\n  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }\n  html, body { width: 100%; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #07090f; font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; }\n  #scene { position: fixed; inset: 0; }\n  canvas { display: block; }\n  #hud {\n    position: fixed; top: 14px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 10;\n    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;\n    background: rgba(14, 16, 26, 0.82); border: 1px solid rgba(210, 180, 255, 0.3);\n    border-radius: 12px; padding: 10px 16px; backdrop-filter: blur(8px);\n    box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); color: #e8ddff; font-size: 14px; user-select: none;\n  }\n  #hud button {\n    background: rgba(160, 110, 255, 0.16); color: #d9c8ff; border: 1px solid rgba(190,150,255,0.4);\n    border-radius: 8px; padding: 5px 11px; font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer; transition: all 0.15s;\n  }\n  #hud button:hover { background: rgba(160,110,255,0.35); color: #fff; transform: translateY(-1px); }\n  #hint { position: fixed; bottom: 18px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 10;\n    color: rgba(200, 185, 230, 0.5); font-size: 12.5px; white-space: nowrap; }\n  #fallback { display: none; position: fixed; inset: 0; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n    color: #ff9c9c; font-size: 16px; padding: 24px; text-align: center; z-index: 20; }\n</style>\n<script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.128.0/examples/js/controls/OrbitControls.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"scene\"></div>\n<div id=\"fallback\">3D unavailable — could not load Three.js (CDN blocked or offline).</div>\n<div id=\"hud\">\n  <span>🌀 Metallic Knot</span>\n  <button id=\"spin\">Pause spin</button>\n  <button id=\"colorBtn\">Recolor</button>\n</div>\n<div id=\"hint\">Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom · Toggle spin / recolor the metal</div>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  'use strict';\n  if (typeof THREE === 'undefined') { document.getElementById('fallback').style.display = 'flex'; return; }\n\n  const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n  scene.background = new THREE.Color(0x07090f);\n  scene.fog = new THREE.Fog(0x07090f, 18, 44);\n\n  const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(45, innerWidth / innerHeight, 0.1, 200);\n  camera.position.set(0, 2.2, 7);\n\n  const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });\n  renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n  renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2));\n  renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\n  renderer.shadowMap.type = THREE.PCFSoftShadowMap;\n  renderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;\n  renderer.outputEncoding = THREE.sRGBEncoding;\n  document.getElementById('scene').appendChild(renderer.domElement);\n\n  const controls = new THREE.OrbitControls(camera, renderer.domElement);\n  controls.enableDamping = true;\n  controls.dampingFactor = 0.08;\n  controls.minDistance = 3.5;\n  controls.maxDistance = 16;\n  controls.target.set(0, 0, 0);\n\n  scene.add(new THREE.AmbientLight(0xffffff, 0.3));\n  const key = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xfff2dd, 1.4);\n  key.position.set(4, 6, 5);\n  key.castShadow = true;\n  key.shadow.mapSize.set(1024, 1024);\n  key.shadow.bias = -0.0004;\n  scene.add(key);\n  const cool = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0x88bbff, 0.5);\n  cool.position.set(-4, 2, -4);\n  scene.add(cool);\n  const back = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xff88aa, 0.3);\n  back.position.set(0, -2, -5);\n  scene.add(back);\n\n  \n  const floor = new THREE.Mesh(\n    new THREE.CircleGeometry(5, 64),\n    new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x0e1018, metalness: 0.6, roughness: 0.35 })\n  );\n  floor.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2;\n  floor.position.y = -1.6;\n  floor.receiveShadow = true;\n  scene.add(floor);\n\n  \n  (function stars() {\n    const n = 1000, pos = new Float32Array(n * 3);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n * 3; i++) pos[i] = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 60;\n    const g = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n    g.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(pos, 3));\n    scene.add(new THREE.Points(g, new THREE.PointsMaterial({ color: 0xffffff, size: 0.09, transparent: true, opacity: 0.75, fog: false })));\n  })();\n\n  const orbitParticles = [];\n  (function orbitDust() {\n    for (let i = 0; i < 140; i++) {\n      const m = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.02, 6, 6),\n        new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0xc9b8ff, transparent: true, opacity: 0.7 }));\n      m.userData = { radius: 2.6 + Math.random() * 1.6, speed: (0.3 + Math.random()) * (Math.random() < 0.5 ? 1 : -1), ph: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2, tilt: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.9 };\n      scene.add(m);\n      orbitParticles.push(m);\n    }\n  })();\n\n  \n  const knotColors = [0xd4af37, 0x66ddff, 0xff77aa, 0x99ff77, 0xbb99ff];\n  let colorIdx = 0;\n  const knot = new THREE.Mesh(\n    new THREE.TorusKnotGeometry(1.1, 0.32, 220, 40, 2, 3),\n    new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: knotColors[0], metalness: 0.92, roughness: 0.18 })\n  );\n  knot.castShadow = true;\n  knot.position.y = 0.4;\n  scene.add(knot);\n\n  document.getElementById('colorBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {\n    colorIdx = (colorIdx + 1) % knotColors.length;\n    knot.material.color.setHex(knotColors[colorIdx]);\n  });\n\n  let spinning = true;\n  document.getElementById('spin').addEventListener('click', () => {\n    spinning = !spinning;\n    document.getElementById('spin').textContent = spinning ? 'Pause spin' : 'Resume spin';\n  });\n\n  window.addEventListener('resize', () => {\n    camera.aspect = innerWidth / innerHeight;\n    camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n    renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n  });\n\n  let t = 0;\n  function animate() {\n    requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n    t += 0.016;\n    if (spinning) {\n      knot.rotation.x += 0.005;\n      knot.rotation.y += 0.012;\n      knot.rotation.z += 0.004;\n    }\n    orbitParticles.forEach(p => {\n      const a = p.userData.ph + t * p.userData.speed;\n      p.position.set(Math.cos(a) * p.userData.radius, Math.sin(a) * p.userData.tilt * 1.2, Math.sin(a) * p.userData.radius);\n    });\n    controls.update();\n    renderer.render(scene, camera);\n  }\n  animate();\n\n  window.__vaca3d = {\n    spinning: () => spinning,\n    color: () => '#' + knot.material.color.getHexString(),\n    recolor: () => { colorIdx = (colorIdx + 1) % knotColors.length; knot.material.color.setHex(knotColors[colorIdx]); },\n  };\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>", "source": "round13:3d-reexposure"}
{"instruction": "Build a 3D bar chart", "input": "Single-file HTML, Three.js r128 via CDN. A 3D data visualization: 12 months of random revenue ($40k-$200k). Bars are BoxGeometry(0.72, 1, 0.72) scaled by value/12, spaced 1.0 apart along X, HSL gradient across months (setHSL(0.55 - t * 0.45, 0.85, 0.55)) with emissive intensity 0.12 for depth. Grow-in animation: scale.y starts 0.001 and eases to 1 over ~1.2s (rebuild restarts it). Hover: Raycaster on pointermove intersects bars, emissiveIntensity jumps 0.12 -> 0.45, HTML tooltip div follows the cursor with <b>Month</b> + value. New Data button regenerates random data and re-animates. Floor grid + axis label sprite, OrbitControls, shadows, resize handler.", "output": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>📊 3D Bar Chart</title>\n<style>\n  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }\n  html, body { width: 100%; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #0b0f18; font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; }\n  #scene { position: fixed; inset: 0; }\n  canvas { display: block; }\n  #hud {\n    position: fixed; top: 14px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 10;\n    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;\n    background: rgba(14, 20, 34, 0.82); border: 1px solid rgba(120, 210, 255, 0.3);\n    border-radius: 12px; padding: 10px 16px; backdrop-filter: blur(8px);\n    box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); color: #dce9ff; font-size: 14px; user-select: none;\n  }\n  #hud button {\n    background: rgba(70, 160, 255, 0.16); color: #c9dcff; border: 1px solid rgba(120,180,255,0.4);\n    border-radius: 8px; padding: 5px 11px; font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer; transition: all 0.15s;\n  }\n  #hud button:hover { background: rgba(70,160,255,0.35); color: #fff; transform: translateY(-1px); }\n  #tooltip {\n    position: fixed; display: none; z-index: 20; pointer-events: none;\n    background: rgba(12, 18, 30, 0.92); border: 1px solid rgba(120, 210, 255, 0.4);\n    border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 12px; color: #dce9ff; font-size: 13px;\n    box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);\n  }\n  #hint { position: fixed; bottom: 18px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 10;\n    color: rgba(170, 195, 230, 0.5); font-size: 12.5px; white-space: nowrap; }\n  #fallback { display: none; position: fixed; inset: 0; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n    color: #ff9c9c; font-size: 16px; padding: 24px; text-align: center; z-index: 20; }\n</style>\n<script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.128.0/examples/js/controls/OrbitControls.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"scene\"></div>\n<div id=\"fallback\">3D unavailable — could not load Three.js (CDN blocked or offline).</div>\n<div id=\"hud\">\n  <span>📊 Revenue</span>\n  <button id=\"newData\">New Data</button>\n</div>\n<div id=\"tooltip\"></div>\n<div id=\"hint\">Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom · Hover a bar for details</div>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  'use strict';\n  if (typeof THREE === 'undefined') { document.getElementById('fallback').style.display = 'flex'; return; }\n\n  const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n  scene.background = new THREE.Color(0x0b0f18);\n  scene.fog = new THREE.Fog(0x0b0f18, 24, 48);\n\n  const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(45, innerWidth / innerHeight, 0.1, 200);\n  camera.position.set(9, 8, 12);\n\n  const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });\n  renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n  renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2));\n  renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\n  renderer.shadowMap.type = THREE.PCFSoftShadowMap;\n  renderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;\n  renderer.outputEncoding = THREE.sRGBEncoding;\n  document.getElementById('scene').appendChild(renderer.domElement);\n\n  const controls = new THREE.OrbitControls(camera, renderer.domElement);\n  controls.enableDamping = true;\n  controls.dampingFactor = 0.08;\n  controls.minDistance = 5;\n  controls.maxDistance = 30;\n  controls.target.set(0, 2, 0);\n\n  scene.add(new THREE.AmbientLight(0x8899bb, 0.55));\n  const key = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 1.1);\n  key.position.set(7, 10, 6);\n  key.castShadow = true;\n  key.shadow.mapSize.set(1024, 1024);\n  key.shadow.bias = -0.0004;\n  scene.add(key);\n  const fill = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0x66aaff, 0.4);\n  fill.position.set(-6, 4, -6);\n  scene.add(fill);\n\n  \n  const grid = new THREE.GridHelper(14, 14, 0x2a3a5c, 0x182338);\n  grid.position.y = 0;\n  scene.add(grid);\n  const base = new THREE.Mesh(\n    new THREE.BoxGeometry(13.5, 0.12, 11),\n    new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x141c2e, roughness: 0.8 })\n  );\n  base.position.y = -0.06;\n  base.receiveShadow = true;\n  scene.add(base);\n\n  (function stars() {\n    const n = 500, pos = new Float32Array(n * 3);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n * 3; i++) pos[i] = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 80;\n    const g = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n    g.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(pos, 3));\n    scene.add(new THREE.Points(g, new THREE.PointsMaterial({ color: 0xffffff, size: 0.1, transparent: true, opacity: 0.6, fog: false })));\n  })();\n\n  \n  const MONTHS = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec'];\n  const barGroup = new THREE.Group();\n  scene.add(barGroup);\n  let bars = [];          \n  let growT = 0;\n\n  function makeData() {\n    return MONTHS.map(m => ({\n      label: m,\n      value: Math.round(40 + Math.random() * 160),\n    }));\n  }\n  let data = makeData();\n\n  function buildBars(animate) {\n    while (barGroup.children.length) barGroup.remove(barGroup.children[0]);\n    bars = [];\n    const n = data.length;\n    const spacing = 1.0;\n    data.forEach((d, i) => {\n      const h = d.value / 12;\n      const w = 0.72;\n      const t = i / Math.max(1, n - 1);\n      const color = new THREE.Color().setHSL(0.55 - t * 0.45, 0.85, 0.55);\n      const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(\n        new THREE.BoxGeometry(w, 1, w),\n        new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: color, metalness: 0.25, roughness: 0.4, emissive: color, emissiveIntensity: 0.12 })\n      );\n      mesh.castShadow = true;\n      mesh.receiveShadow = true;\n      mesh.position.set((i - (n - 1) / 2) * spacing, h / 2, 0);\n      mesh.scale.y = animate ? 0.001 : 1;\n      mesh.userData = { label: d.label, value: d.value, targetY: h };\n      barGroup.add(mesh);\n      bars.push(mesh);\n    });\n  }\n  buildBars(true);\n\n  \n  const raycaster = new THREE.Raycaster();\n  const pointer = new THREE.Vector2();\n  const tooltip = document.getElementById('tooltip');\n  let hoveredBar = null;\n\n  renderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => {\n    const rect = renderer.domElement.getBoundingClientRect();\n    pointer.x = ((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 2 - 1;\n    pointer.y = -((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * 2 + 1;\n    raycaster.setFromCamera(pointer, camera);\n    const hit = raycaster.intersectObjects(bars)[0];\n    if (hit) {\n      const u = hit.object.userData;\n      tooltip.style.display = 'block';\n      tooltip.style.left = (e.clientX + 14) + 'px';\n      tooltip.style.top = (e.clientY - 10) + 'px';\n      tooltip.innerHTML = `<b>${u.label}</b><br>$${u.value}k`;\n      if (hoveredBar !== hit.object) {\n        if (hoveredBar) hoveredBar.material.emissiveIntensity = 0.12;\n        hoveredBar = hit.object;\n        hoveredBar.material.emissiveIntensity = 0.45;\n      }\n    } else {\n      tooltip.style.display = 'none';\n      if (hoveredBar) { hoveredBar.material.emissiveIntensity = 0.12; hoveredBar = null; }\n    }\n  });\n\n  document.getElementById('newData').addEventListener('click', () => {\n    data = makeData();\n    buildBars(true);\n    growT = 0;\n  });\n\n  window.addEventListener('resize', () => {\n    camera.aspect = innerWidth / innerHeight;\n    camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n    renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n  });\n\n  \n  function animate() {\n    requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n    if (growT < 1) {\n      growT = Math.min(1, growT + 0.02);\n      const k = growT < 0.5 ? 2 * growT * growT : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * growT + 2, 2) / 2;\n      bars.forEach(b => {\n        b.scale.y = Math.max(0.001, k);\n        b.position.y = (b.userData.targetY / 2) * k;\n      });\n    }\n    controls.update();\n    renderer.render(scene, camera);\n  }\n  animate();\n\n  window.__vaca3d = {\n    bars: () => bars.length,\n    values: () => bars.map(b => b.userData.value),\n    newData: () => { data = makeData(); buildBars(true); growT = 0; },\n  };\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>", "source": "round13:3d-reexposure"}
{"instruction": "Implement chess rules with check detection", "input": "Plain JavaScript chess rules: 8x8 board state, per-piece pseudo-legal moves with capture/en-passant/double-pawn flags, isAttacked with sliding-piece + knight + pawn attack checks, legal moves filtered by king safety (apply/undo), castling rights, auto-queen promotion, and a depth-2 minimax with material evaluation for the AI. Critical: applyMove must save the captured piece (mv.capture flag) so undoMove restores it — otherwise minimax corrupts the board.", "output": "function legalFrom(r, c) {\n  const p = boardState[r][c]; if (!p) return [];\n  const out = [];\n  for (const mv of pseudoLegal(r, c)) {\n    const target = applyMove(r, c, mv);\n    const ok = !inCheck(p.color);\n    undoMove(r, c, mv, target);\n    if (ok) out.push(mv);\n  }\n  return out;\n}\nfunction applyMove(r, c, mv) {\n  const p = boardState[r][c];\n  const target = mv.capture ? boardState[mv.r][mv.c] : null;\n  if (mv.enPassant) { const pr = mv.r + (p.color === 'white' ? 1 : -1); boardState[pr][mv.c] = null; }\n  if (mv.castle === 'k') { const h = p.color === 'white' ? 7 : 0; boardState[h][5] = boardState[h][7]; boardState[h][7] = null; }\n  if (mv.castle === 'q') { const h = p.color === 'white' ? 7 : 0; boardState[h][3] = boardState[h][0]; boardState[h][0] = null; }\n  boardState[mv.r][mv.c] = p;\n  boardState[r][c] = null;\n  return target;\n}\nfunction undoMove(r, c, mv, target) {\n  const p = boardState[mv.r][mv.c];\n  boardState[r][c] = p;\n  boardState[mv.r][mv.c] = target !== undefined ? target : null;\n  if (mv.enPassant) { const pr = mv.r + (p.color === 'white' ? 1 : -1); boardState[pr][mv.c] = { type: 'pawn', color: p.color === 'white' ? 'black' : 'white' }; }\n  if (mv.castle === 'k') { const h = p.color === 'white' ? 7 : 0; boardState[h][7] = boardState[h][5]; boardState[h][5] = null; }\n  if (mv.castle === 'q') { const h = p.color === 'white' ? 7 : 0; boardState[h][0] = boardState[h][3]; boardState[h][3] = null; }\n}\nfunction minimax(depth, isMax) {\n  const color = isMax ? 'white' : 'black';\n  const moves = allLegal(color);\n  if (moves.length === 0) return isMax ? -99999 : 99999;\n  if (depth === 0) return evaluate();\n  let best = isMax ? -Infinity : Infinity;\n  for (const { r, c, mv } of moves) {\n    const target = applyMove(r, c, mv);\n    const v = minimax(depth - 1, !isMax);\n    undoMove(r, c, mv, target);\n    if (isMax) best = Math.max(best, v); else best = Math.min(best, v);\n  }\n  return best;\n}", "source": "round13:3d-reexposure"}
{"instruction": "Build a 3D butterfly swarm", "input": "Single-file HTML, Three.js r128 via CDN. 140 butterflies: each is a group of two wing meshes (BufferGeometry pair of triangles, DoubleSide) that FLAP (rotation.y oscillates) while wandering on per-butterfly Lissajous-ish paths (cos/sin with per-item radius, speed, phase, amplitude) around the origin, lookAt the center. Butterflies cloned from a shared template; Respawn rebuilds the swarm. HemisphereLight green-ish + sun with shadows, fog. OrbitControls, dt-guarded loop, resize.", "output": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>3D Butterfly Swarm</title>\n<style>\n  html,body{margin:0;height:100%;overflow:hidden;background:#0b0e14;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;}\n  #scene{position:fixed;inset:0;}\n  #hud{position:fixed;top:12px;left:12px;z-index:10;color:#e8ecf4;background:rgba(10,14,22,.72);padding:10px 14px;border-radius:10px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;backdrop-filter:blur(4px);pointer-events:none;max-width:46vw;}\n  #hud b{color:#ffd479;}\n  .btn{position:fixed;z-index:10;bottom:16px;background:#2a3450;color:#e8ecf4;border:1px solid #46527a;padding:9px 16px;border-radius:9px;font-size:13px;cursor:pointer;transition:transform .12s,background .12s;}\n  .btn:hover{background:#3a4670;transform:translateY(-1px);}\n  .btn:active{transform:translateY(1px);}\n  \n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"scene\"></div>\n<div id=\"hud\"></div>\n<div id=\"btns\"></div>\n<script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.128.0/examples/js/controls/OrbitControls.js\"></script>\n<script>\n    if (!window.THREE) {\n      document.getElementById('hud').textContent = 'Failed to load Three.js (check network)';\n      throw new Error('THREE missing');\n    }\n\n    function mkBtn(id, label, fn) {\n      const b = document.createElement('button');\n      b.id = id; b.className = 'btn'; b.textContent = label;\n      b.style.left = '16px'; b.style.bottom = '16px';\n      document.getElementById('btns').appendChild(b);\n      b.addEventListener('click', fn);\n    }\n\n    const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n    scene.background = new THREE.Color(0x0b0e14);\n    const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(45, innerWidth / innerHeight, 0.1, 400);\n    const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });\n    renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n    renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2));\n    renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true;\n    renderer.shadowMap.type = THREE.PCFSoftShadowMap;\n    renderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;\n    renderer.outputEncoding = THREE.sRGBEncoding;\n    document.getElementById('scene').appendChild(renderer.domElement);\n    const controls = new THREE.OrbitControls(camera, renderer.domElement);\n    controls.enableDamping = true; controls.dampingFactor = 0.08;\n    controls.maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.92;\n    let last = 0;\n    function loop(now) {\n      requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n      const dt = last ? Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.05) : 0.016;\n      last = now;\n      tick(dt, now / 1000);\n      controls.update();\n      renderer.render(scene, camera);\n    }\n    window.addEventListener('resize', () => {\n      camera.aspect = innerWidth / innerHeight;\n      camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n      renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n    });\n\n    const hud = document.getElementById('hud');\n    hud.innerHTML = '🦋 <b>Butterfly Swarm</b> — drag to orbit · respawn';\n    camera.position.set(0, 7, 15);\n    scene.background = new THREE.Color(0x17221a);\n    scene.fog = new THREE.Fog(0x17221a, 30, 80);\n\n    const N = 140;\n    \n    const wingGeo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n    wingGeo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([\n      -0.75, 0, 0,  0, 0, 0,  -0.75, 0, -0.5,\n       0.75, 0, 0,  0, 0, 0,   0.75, 0, -0.5,\n    ], 3));\n    wingGeo.computeVertexNormals();\n    const wingMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({\n      color: 0xff9ad5, roughness: 0.4, side: THREE.DoubleSide, transparent: true, opacity: 0.92,\n    });\n    const butterfly = new THREE.Group();\n    const wl = new THREE.Mesh(wingGeo, wingMat); wl.position.x = -0.3;\n    const wr = new THREE.Mesh(wingGeo, wingMat); wr.position.x = 0.3;\n    butterfly.add(wl, wr);\n\n    let swarm = new THREE.Group();\n    function buildSwarm() {\n      scene.remove(swarm);\n      swarm.traverse(o => { if (o.geometry) o.geometry.dispose(); });\n      swarm = new THREE.Group();\n      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n        const b = butterfly.clone();\n        b.userData = {\n          ph: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2, spd: 0.6 + Math.random() * 1.1,\n          r: 2 + Math.random() * 5, amp: 1.4 + Math.random() * 2.2,\n          hue: Math.random(), flap: 0.25 + Math.random() * 0.5,\n        };\n        swarm.add(b);\n      }\n      scene.add(swarm);\n    }\n    buildSwarm();\n    mkBtn('b-butter', '🦋 Respawn swarm', () => buildSwarm());\n\n    scene.add(new THREE.HemisphereLight(0xbfe8d0, 0x1a2a20, 0.8));\n    const sun = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xfff0d8, 0.85);\n    sun.position.set(12, 18, 8); sun.castShadow = true;\n    scene.add(sun);\n\n    function tick(dt, t) {\n      for (const b of swarm.children) {\n        const u = b.userData;\n        const ang = t * u.spd + u.ph;\n        b.position.set(Math.cos(ang) * u.r, 3 + Math.sin(ang * 1.7 + u.ph) * u.amp, Math.sin(ang * 1.3) * u.r);\n        b.lookAt(0, 2, 0);\n        const flap = Math.sin(t * 9 * u.flap + u.ph) * 0.75;\n        b.children[0].rotation.y = flap;\n        b.children[1].rotation.y = -flap;\n      }\n      void dt;\n    }\n    window.__vaca3d = { butterflies: N };\n    \n\n    loop(0);\n\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>", "source": "round13:random-3d"}
{"instruction": "Animate 3D piece movement with lerp", "input": "Three.js r128. Smoothly move a piece mesh from square A to square B with position.lerpVectors + easeInOut inside the render loop; animate a captured piece flying up and fading; support castling (also move the rook) and en passant. Add a Raycaster for square picking and flat highlight planes for legal moves.", "output": "const anims = [];\nfunction easeInOut(k) { return k < 0.5 ? 2 * k * k : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * k + 2, 2) / 2; }\nfunction animateMove(from, to, mesh) {\n  const p0 = squarePos(from.r, from.c), p1 = squarePos(to.r, to.c);\n  mesh.position.set(p0.x, p0.y, p0.z);\n  anims.push({ mesh: mesh, from: p0, to: p1, t: 0, dur: 420 });\n}\n// in the render loop:\nfor (let i = anims.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n  const a = anims[i];\n  a.t += 16.67 / a.dur;\n  const k = easeInOut(Math.min(a.t, 1));\n  a.mesh.position.lerpVectors(a.from, a.to, k);\n  if (a.t >= 1) { if (a.onDone) a.onDone(); anims.splice(i, 1); }\n}\n// picking:\nconst raycaster = new THREE.Raycaster();\nconst pointer = new THREE.Vector2();\nrenderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointerdown', function (e) {\n  const rect = renderer.domElement.getBoundingClientRect();\n  pointer.x = ((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 2 - 1;\n  pointer.y = -((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * 2 + 1;\n  raycaster.setFromCamera(pointer, camera);\n  const hit = raycaster.intersectObject(pickPlane)[0];\n  if (hit) { const r = Math.round(hit.point.z + 3.5), c = Math.round(hit.point.x + 3.5); /* select/move */ }\n});", "source": "round13:3d-reexposure"}
{"instruction": "a python script named main.py that writes the note 'Hello Note' to a file named notes.txt, reads it back, and prints the content", "input": "", "output": "# ===== main.py =====\n```python\nimport os\n\nfilename = 'notes.txt'\ndef write_note(text):\n    with open(filename, 'w') as f:\n        f.write(text)\ndef read_note():\n    if os.path.exists(filename):\n        with open(filename, 'r') as f:\n            return f.read()\n    return ''\n\nwrite_note('Hello Note')\nprint(read_note())\n```", "source": "round13:retention-r12", "at": "2026-08-09T01:51:01.975311Z"}
{"instruction": "Build terrain geometry in Three.js r128", "input": "THREE.Geometry, geometry.vertices and THREE.Face3 were removed in r125+. Build meshes with BufferGeometry: position attribute, indices, computeVertexNormals.", "output": "const geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\nconst positionsArr = [];\nconst indicesArr = [];\nfor (let x = 0; x < size - 1; x++) {\n  for (let y = 0; y < size - 1; y++) {\n    const i0 = positionsArr.length / 3;\n    positionsArr.push(x, h[x][y], y, x + 1, h[x + 1][y], y, x + 1, h[x + 1][y + 1], y + 1, x, h[x][y + 1], y + 1);\n    indicesArr.push(i0, i0 + 1, i0 + 2, i0, i0 + 2, i0 + 3);\n  }\n}\ngeometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(positionsArr, 3));\ngeometry.setIndex(indicesArr);\ngeometry.computeVertexNormals();", "source": "round13:defects-reexposure"}
{"instruction": "Orient a cylinder along a 3D vector (bonds, struts)", "input": "Three.js r128. For a bond/strut between two points: compute midpoint, length, and direction, then scale.y = length and quaternion.setFromUnitVectors(new THREE.Vector3(0,1,0), dir). Works for molecule bonds, antennae, cables, spider legs.", "output": "function strut(a, b, geo, mat) {\n  const mid = new THREE.Vector3().addVectors(a, b).multiplyScalar(0.5);\n  const dir = new THREE.Vector3().subVectors(b, a);\n  const m = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\n  m.scale.y = dir.length();\n  m.position.copy(mid);\n  m.quaternion.setFromUnitVectors(new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0), dir.clone().normalize());\n  return m;\n}", "source": "round13:random-3d"}
